      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the recent SCOTUS ruling in New York State Rifle & Pistol Association v. Bruen (2022) did strike down the nearly century-old \"Issenmann\" precedent and somewhat relaxed the requirements for gun 'concealed carry' laws, it does not necessarily render all strict gun control measures unconstitutional. The Court maintained that the Second Amendment protects an individual's right to bear armed self-defense outside the home, but allowed for regulatory measures that do not unduly burden this right. This gives opponents of strict gun control some breathing room, but it's still unclear whether these measures must now be deemed unconstitutional under specific circumstances.",
